.TH "BBR\-LINKS" "1" "November 2026" "bbr\-tools 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bbr\-links \- list network interfaces and watch link changes using
rtnetlink
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]bbr\-links\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-watch\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]bbr\-links\f[R] asks the kernel for every network interface over an
rtnetlink socket (an \f[B]RTM_GETLINK\f[R] dump request) and prints one
line per interface: index, name, state, MTU, link\-layer address, and
received and transmitted packet counts.
.PP
The state is \f[B]UP\f[R] when the interface is administratively up and
has carrier, \f[B]NO\-CARRIER\f[R] when it is up but no cable or link
partner is detected, and \f[B]DOWN\f[R] when it is administratively
down.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-watch\f[R]
After printing the list, join the \f[B]RTMGRP_LINK\f[R] multicast group
and print a time\-stamped line whenever an interface changes state,
appears or is removed.
Runs until interrupted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\f[B]0\f[R] on success, \f[B]1\f[R] if the netlink socket cannot be
created, bound or used.
.SH EXAMPLES
List interfaces:
.IP
.EX
bbr\-links
.EE
.PP
Watch the WAN link while unplugging its cable:
.IP
.EX
bbr\-links \-\-watch
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]ip\-link\f[R](8), \f[B]netlink\f[R](7), \f[B]rtnetlink\f[R](7)
